E AX3060 1033-recover-escape.ax:22:10-17 region-escape "a value allocated in the recovery point (reclaimed on abort) is stored into parameter `v` of `vecPush`, which lives in this function's own region (its caller's current region) - `vecPush` stores a value it allocates into that parameter" ?"MM-RGN-3 (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md): a value may be stored only into a place its own region OUTLIVES, because the place is still readable after the value's region has been reclaimed. A region named in a signature (`@r`) outlives the function's own region and is unordered against another name; the function's own region is its caller's. Keep the value in the region of the place it is stored into - allocate it there, or copy it there - or widen the place's annotation to the value's region"
E AX3090 1033-recover-escape.ax:31:6-21 recover-thunk-unseen "a recovery point's thunk has to be a lambda written at the call, or a top-level function" ?"an abort reclaims everything the thunk allocated, so the thunk is held to storing none of it anywhere older; that is checked on a lambda written here, and a top-level function captures nothing. Write the lambda at the call"
